$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(3-Chloro-5-(4-morpholin-4yl-phenyl)pyridin-4-yl)piperidine-4-carbonitrile
(40): 1-(3-Bromo-5-chloropyridin-4-yl)piperidine-4-carbonitrile 39 (30
mg, 0.10 mmol), 4-N-morpholinophenylboronic acid (23 mg, 0.11 mmol) and
Pd(dppf)Cl2.CH2Cl2 (4.1 mg, 5.0 μmol) were loaded in a microwave vial and
purged with nitrogen. Acetonitrile (1 mL) and 0.5 M aqueous sodium
carbonate solution (0.275 mL, 0.138 mmol) were added and the reaction
mixture heated under microwave irradiation at 120 °C for 1 h. Once
cooled, the reaction mixture was evaporated onto silica gel and purified
by flash chromatography (EtOAc/cHex 1:10 to 1:1). The title compound 40
(31 mg, 81% yield) as a white solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.79-1.92
(m, 4H), 2.66-2.74 (m, 1H), 2.76-2.86 (m, 2H), 3.03-3.11 (m, 2H),
3.21-3.26 (m, 4H), 3.86-3.92 (m, 4H), 6.97-7.00 (m, 2H), 7.15-7.18 (m,
2H), 8.21 (s, 1H), 8.42 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 26.1, 28.9,
48.8, 49.2, 66.8, 115.3, 121.3, 128.1, 128.3, 130.0, 134.1, 149.1, 150.8,
150.9, 152.3; LC (Method C) - MS (ESI, m/z) Rt = 2.45 min – 383/385
(M+H)+. ESIHRMS: Found: 405.1439 calculated for C21H23 35ClN4NaO (M+Na)+:
405.1453.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Potent, Orally Bioavailable, Small-Molecule Inhibitors of
WNT Signaling from a Cell-Based Pathway Screen
