$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for syntheses of
6-chloro-7-aryl-deazapurines (Cross Coupling): To
7-substituted-4-chloro-5-iodo-pyrrolopyrimidine (1.0 equiv.) in a 6 dram
vial was added aryl boronic acid (1.5 equiv.), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.05 equiv.),
and Na2CO3 (2.5 equiv.). The mixture was thoroughly purged with argon and
then dissolved in a 3:1 mixture of degassed dioxane and degassed water
until the mixture was 0.2 M in pyrrolopyrimidine. The mixture was then
let stir for 18 h at 80 °C upon which time the mixture was partitioned
between 5 mL water and 5 mL ethyl acetate. The organic layers were
separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted two more times with ethyl
acetate. The organic layers were combined, dried with Na2SO4, and
concentrated down. A crude oil which was purified by FCC (hexanes:ethyl
acetate: 40:1 to 8:1) to yield pure product.
7-(tert-butyl)-4-chloro-5-(2-trifluoromethyl)phenylpyrrolopyrimidine
(Substrate for 10): 76% isolated yield as a yellow oil. R f : 0.30 (9:1
hexanes:ethyl acetate); 1H NMR (599 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.65 (s, 1H), 7.77 (d,
J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.57 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.51 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.44
(d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 7.36 (s, 1H), 1.83 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 152.10, 150.95, 149.58, 134.48, 132.38 (q, J = 1.7 Hz), 130.84, 130.58
(q, J = 29 Hz), 128.03, 126.70, 125.88 (q, J = 5.2 Hz), 124.57 (q, J =
274 Hz), 117.43, 110.76, 58.18, 29.43; 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3) δ -57.20
(referenced to an external trifluoroacetic acid standard); MS (ESI):
Calculated C17H16ClF3N3 + [M+H] 354.0979. Found: 354.0976 m/z.
